module

public import CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter3.Section01.CommonNormalKnownSimple
public import CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter15.Section04.Centralizer.Preliminaries.RatioSource.CommonNormal

/-!
# The common-normal source input for the Chapter 15 ratio argument

The proved known-simple Theorem 3.1.1 supplies a nontrivial subgroup of the
original R normal in the group generated by A and H. Its ambient Sylow,
unique maximal overgroup and residual-Sylow hypotheses agree exactly with
`Earlier311`. This adapter instantiates that source implication while keeping
the actual ambient group and subgroup inclusions.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, Theorem 3.1.1, printed pp.571–572, and its
application in 15.4.2(4), printed p.1156.
-/

public section

namespace CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter15.Section04.RatioSource

universe u
variable {G : Type u} [Group G] [Finite G]

/-- The original common-normal source implication, with C.5.8 and every
earlier classification premise discharged on the full known-simple class. -/
theorem source_earlier311_knownSimple : Earlier311 (G := G) :=
  fun T hG => Chapter3.source_common_normal_knownSimple hG T

end CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter15.Section04.RatioSource
